IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`
IMPORT `sgta-i-rg3-licences`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 3): the seven amending instruments in IMDA's list, each in its
-- own section, with its commencement date as the date edge: S 61/2003 (10 February 2003), S 166/2003 (1 April 2003), S 565/2004 (8 September
-- 2004), S 476/2005 (21 July 2005), S 76/2007 (1 March 2007), S 110/2008 (1 March 2008), S 685/2011 (28 December 2011).
-- Texts: TA1999-RG3-S61-2003 and the others under subjects/sg/telecommunications-class-licences-regulations-2000/registers/source-bundle/.
-- S 685/2011: IMDA's copy has no text layer, so its deposited text was OCR, with misreadings ("J." for "1.", "74." for "7A.", "reference and inserting" for "references and substituting").
-- On 2026-11-04 the e-Gazette's copy, which has a text layer, replaced it as TA1999-RG3-S685-2011.txt; the OCR text is kept as TA1999-RG3-S685-2011-OCR.txt and is not quoted.
-- Every quotation of S 685/2011 below is from the Gazette text; the encoded rules did not change (the fees, the dates and the wording they rest on are the same in both).
-- Each rule is the amended provision in its new form and answers NOTHING before the amending instrument's commencement.  Reg 3 itself,
-- in its 2002 and 2011 forms, is in sgta-i-rg3-class.l4.

§ `S 61/2003 (in operation 10 February 2003)`

-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:14 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Class Licences)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:15 | (Amendment) Regulations 2003 and shall come into operation on 10th February 2003.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:17 | Amendment of Third Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:18 | 2. The Third Schedule to the Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:19 | (Rg 3) (referred to in these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:20 | (a) by deleting paragraph 1 and substituting the following paragraphs:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:21 | “1. The telecommunication services specified in paragraph 1A may
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:22 | be resold under this class licence where they are provided through —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:23 | (a) an FBO who is licensed to provide public basic
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:24 | telecommunication services, public cellular mobile telephone
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:25 | services or public radio paging services; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:26 | (b) an SBO who is licensed to provide international simple
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:27 | resale, mobile virtual network operation, international calling
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:28 | card services, internet based voice and data services, or call-
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:29 | back and call re-origination services.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:30 | 1A. The telecommunication services referred to in paragraph 1 are the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:31 | following public switched telecommunication services (whether
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:32 | domestic or international):
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:33 | (a) public switched telephone services, other than public chain
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:34 | payphone services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:35 | (b) public cellular mobile telephone services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:36 | (c) public radio paging services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:37 | (d) public switched message services;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:38 | (e) public switched data services; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:39 | (f) public integrated services digital network services.”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:40 | (b) by inserting, immediately after “FBO” in paragraphs 5 and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:41 | 8, the words “or SBO”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:43 | Amendment of Fourth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:44 | 3. The Fourth Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:45 | (a) by inserting, immediately after “FBO” in paragraph 5, the words “or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:46 | SBO”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:47 | (b) by deleting paragraph 10 and substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:48 | “10. A licensee may only resell the services of —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:49 | (a) an FBO who is licensed to provide public basic
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:50 | telecommunication services, public cellular mobile telephone
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:51 | services or public radio paging services; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:52 | (b) an SBO who is licensed to provide international simple
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:53 | resale, mobile virtual network operation, international calling
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:54 | card services, internet based voice and data services, or call-
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:55 | back and call re-origination services,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:56 | and not those of any other licensee.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:58 | Amendment of Seventh Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:59 | 4. Paragraph 1 of the Seventh Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended by
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:60 | deleting “PIN” and substituting the words “Personal Identification Number (PIN)”.
@ref Rg 3 as amended by S 61/2003 (src:TA1999-RG3-S61-2003:14-60)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the service is provided through an FBO licensed for public basic telecommunication services, public cellular mobile telephone services or public radio paging services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is provided through an SBO licensed for international simple resale, mobile virtual network operation, international calling card services, internet based voice and data services, or call-back and call re-origination services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Third Schedule item 1 (from 10 February 2003): the telecommunication services in paragraph 1A may be resold under the class licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 10 2 2003) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the service is provided through an FBO licensed for public basic telecommunication services, public cellular mobile telephone services or public radio paging services` OR `the service is provided through an SBO licensed for international simple resale, mobile virtual network operation, international calling card services, internet based voice and data services, or call-back and call re-origination services`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee resells only the services of an FBO or an SBO of the kinds paragraph 10 names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Fourth Schedule item 10 (from 10 February 2003): the licensee is meeting the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 10 2 2003) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the licensee resells only the services of an FBO or an SBO of the kinds paragraph 10 names`

§ `S 166/2003 (in operation 1 April 2003)`

-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:15 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Class Licences)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:16 | (Amendment No. 2) Regulations 2003 and shall come into operation on 1st April 2003.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:18 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 11
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:19 | 2. Regulation 11 of the Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations (Rg 3) is
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:20 | deleted and the following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:21 | “Provision of prepaid services
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:22 | 11. No licensee shall collect money deposits or use prepaid cards (other than
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:23 | credit cards) as a means of collecting payment from its customers.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:25 | Transitional provision
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:26 | 3. Notwithstanding regulation 2, any licensee —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:27 | (a) whose licence is granted before 1st April 2003; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:28 | (b) who, before that date, has been collecting money deposits or using prepaid
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:29 | cards (other than credit cards) as a means of collecting payment from its
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:30 | customers,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:31 | may continue to do so until 30th September 2003, subject however to the condition that
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:32 | it must take such measures as the Authority considers necessary to ensure that it is able
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:33 | to refund any balance due to such customers in the event of default in the provision of
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:34 | its services.
@ref Rg 3 as amended by S 166/2003 (src:TA1999-RG3-S166-2003:15-34)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee collects money deposits or uses prepaid cards (other than credit cards) as a means of collecting payment from its customers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence was granted before 1 April 2003 and the licensee was already collecting deposits or using prepaid cards before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee takes the measures the Authority considers necessary to ensure it can refund any balance due on default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 11 (from 1 April 2003): the licensee may collect money deposits or use prepaid cards` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 4 2003) THEN NOTHING
           IF NOT `the licensee collects money deposits or uses prepaid cards (other than credit cards) as a means of collecting payment from its customers` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 10 2003) THEN JUST (`the licence was granted before 1 April 2003 and the licensee was already collecting deposits or using prepaid cards before that date` AND `the licensee takes the measures the Authority considers necessary to ensure it can refund any balance due on default`)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `S 565/2004 (in operation 8 September 2004)`

-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:14 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Class Licences)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:15 | (Amendment) Regulations 2004 and shall come into operation on 8th September 2004.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:17 | Amendment of First Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:18 | 2. The First Schedule to the Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations (Rg 3)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:19 | (referred to in these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is amended by inserting,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:20 | immediately after paragraph 4, the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:21 | “5. A licensee must publish its name as registered with the Accounting and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:22 | Corporate Regulatory Authority in any advertisement of its services.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:24 | Amendment of Second Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:25 | 3. The Second Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended by inserting,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:26 | immediately after paragraph 10, the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:27 | “11. A licensee must publish its name as registered with the Accounting and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:28 | Corporate Regulatory Authority in any advertisement of its services.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:30 | Amendment of Fifth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:31 | 4. Paragraph 1 of the Fifth Schedule to the principal Regulations is deleted and the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:32 | following paragraph substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:33 | “1. Call-back and call re-origination services are International Direct Dial
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:34 | (IDD) call reversal services passing over any FBO’s international telephone
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:35 | gateway and public switched telecommunication network or local call reversal
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:36 | services passing over any FBO's public switched telecommunication network.”.
@ref Rg 3 as amended by S 565/2004 (src:TA1999-RG3-S565-2004:14-36)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee publishes its name as registered with the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority in any advertisement of its services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 First Schedule item 5 and Second Schedule item 11 (from 8 September 2004): the licensee is meeting the condition on advertisements` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 8 9 2004) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the licensee publishes its name as registered with the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority in any advertisement of its services`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the service is International Direct Dial call reversal passing over an FBO's international gateway and public switched network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service is local call reversal passing over an FBO's public switched telecommunication network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Fifth Schedule item 1 (from 8 September 2004): this is a call-back or call re-origination service` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 8 9 2004) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the service is International Direct Dial call reversal passing over an FBO's international gateway and public switched network` OR `the service is local call reversal passing over an FBO's public switched telecommunication network`)

§ `S 476/2005 (in operation 21 July 2005)`

-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:14 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Class Licences)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:15 | (Amendment) Regulations 2005 and shall come into operation on 21st July 2005.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:17 | Amendment of regulation 5
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:18 | 2. Regulation 5 of the Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations (Rg 3)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:19 | (referred to in these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is amended by deleting the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:20 | words “or renewal of registration, as the case may be,”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:22 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 6
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:23 | 3. Regulation 6 of the principal Regulations is deleted and the following regulation
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:24 | substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:25 | “Duration and cancellation of licence
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:26 | 6. —(1) A class licence shall remain valid unless it is cancelled in accordance
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:27 | with the provisions of the Act or these Regulations.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:28 | (2) The Authority may cancel a class licence where the holder of such licence —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:29 | (a) gives notice to the Authority in such form and manner as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:30 | may determine that he has ceased to be an operator; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:31 | (b) has ceased to carry on any business or trade as an operator and the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:32 | registration of the business under the Business Registration Act (Cap. 32)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:33 | is cancelled; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:34 | (c) being a company incorporated under the Companies Act (Cap. 50) or a
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:35 | limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:36 | Partnerships Act 2005 (Act 5 of 2005), has gone into liquidation other
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:37 | than for the purpose of amalgamation or reconstruction.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:38 | (3) A cancellation of a class licence of a person shall not operate so as to —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:39 | (a) prejudice any liability incurred by such person under these Regulations
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:40 | and any such liability may be enforced against him as if the cancellation
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:41 | had not taken place; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:42 | (b) prevent such person from subsequently being deemed a holder of such
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:43 | licence under these Regulations.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:45 | New regulation 12A
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:46 | 4. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately after regulation 12,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:47 | the following regulation:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:48 | “Usage, etc., of telephone numbers
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:49 | 12A. It is a condition of every class licence that the licensee must comply with
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:50 | the Authority’s —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:51 | (a) National Numbering Plan; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:52 | (b) framework and guidelines on the usage, allocation and assignment of
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:53 | numbers.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:55 | Amendment of Eighth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:56 | 5. The Eighth Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:57 | (a) by deleting the words “for 3 years” wherever they appear in Part I; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:58 | (b) by deleting the words “for every 3 years” in Part II.
@ref Rg 3 as amended by S 476/2005 (src:TA1999-RG3-S476-2005:14-58)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the operator paid the fee, if any, that the Eighth Schedule specifies, on registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 5 (from 21 July 2005): the operator has paid the registration fee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the operator paid the fee, if any, that the Eighth Schedule specifies, on registration`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the holder gave notice in the form and manner the Authority determined that it has ceased to be an operator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder has ceased to carry on any business or trade as an operator and the registration of the business under the Business Registration Act is cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the holder, a company or a limited liability partnership, has gone into liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 6(2) (from 21 July 2005): the Authority may cancel the class licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the holder gave notice in the form and manner the Authority determined that it has ceased to be an operator` OR `the holder has ceased to carry on any business or trade as an operator and the registration of the business under the Business Registration Act is cancelled` OR `the holder, a company or a limited liability partnership, has gone into liquidation other than for amalgamation or reconstruction`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 6(1) and (3) (from 21 July 2005): the class licence remains valid unless cancelled, and a cancellation leaves liability incurred enforceable` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee complies with the Authority's National Numbering Plan and its framework and guidelines on the usage, allocation and assignment of numbers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 12A (from 21 July 2005): the licensee has met the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the licensee complies with the Authority's National Numbering Plan and its framework and guidelines on the usage, allocation and assignment of numbers`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Eighth Schedule (from 21 July 2005): the registration fees are stated without a period ("for 3 years" and "for every 3 years" deleted)` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `S 76/2007 (in operation 1 March 2007)`

-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:16 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Class Licences)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:17 | (Amendment) Regulations 2007 and shall come into operation on 1st March 2007.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:19 | Amendment of Third Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:20 | 2. The Third Schedule to the Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations (Rg 3)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:21 | is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:22 | (a) by inserting, immediately after the words “public chain payphone services” in
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:23 | paragraph 1A (a), the words “and services exempted from licensing under the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:24 | Telecommunications (Exemption of Resellers of Local Calls Operating Coinafons
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:25 | or Payphones) Notification 2007 (G.N. No. S 77/2007)”;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:26 | (b) by deleting paragraph 5 and substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:27 | “5. A licensee must not charge its users a usage rate higher than the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:28 | published rate for an equivalent or a similar service provided by the FBO
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:29 | or SBO through which it provides its services.”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:30 | (c) by inserting, immediately after the words “its users” in paragraph 9, the words
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:31 | “except users of an international payphone service provided by the licensee in any
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:32 | single customer premises”.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:34 | Amendment of Fourth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:35 | 3. The Fourth Schedule to the Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations is
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:36 | amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:37 | (a) by inserting, immediately after the words “public switched telephone services”
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:38 | in paragraph 1, the words “but does not include services exempted from licensing
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:39 | under the Telecommunications (Exemption of Resellers of Local Calls Operating
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:40 | Coinafons or Payphones) Notification 2007 (G.N. No. S 77/2007)”; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:41 | (b) by deleting paragraph 5 and substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:42 | “5. A licensee must not charge its users a usage rate higher than the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:43 | published rate for an equivalent or a similar service provided by the FBO
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:44 | or SBO through which it provides its services.”.
@ref Rg 3 as amended by S 76/2007 (src:TA1999-RG3-S76-2007:16-44)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the service is a public switched telephone service other than public chain payphone services and services exempted under the Telecommunications (Exemption of Resellers of Local Calls Operating Coinafons or Payphones) Notification 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Third Schedule paragraph 1A(a) (from 1 March 2007): this is a public switched telephone service that may be resold` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 3 2007) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the service is a public switched telephone service other than public chain payphone services and services exempted under the Telecommunications (Exemption of Resellers of Local Calls Operating Coinafons or Payphones) Notification 2007`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the usage rate charged exceeds the published rate for an equivalent or similar service provided by the FBO or SBO through which the licensee provides its services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Third Schedule paragraph 5 and Fourth Schedule paragraph 5 (from 1 March 2007): the licensee may charge its users the rate` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 3 2007) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (NOT `the usage rate charged exceeds the published rate for an equivalent or similar service provided by the FBO or SBO through which the licensee provides its services`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the user is a user of an international payphone service provided by the licensee in a single customer premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has a written service agreement with the user` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Third Schedule paragraph 9 (from 1 March 2007): the licensee is meeting the condition for this user` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 3 2007) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the user is a user of an international payphone service provided by the licensee in a single customer premises` OR `the licensee has a written service agreement with the user`)

§ `S 110/2008 (in operation 1 March 2008)`

-- src:TA1999-RG3-S110-2008:16 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Class Licences)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S110-2008:17 | (Amendment) Regulations 2008 and shall come into operation on 1st March 2008.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S110-2008:19 | Amendment of Third Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S110-2008:20 | 2. The Third Schedule to the Telecommunications (Class Licences) Regulations (Rg 3) is
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S110-2008:21 | amended by deleting paragraphs 5 and 6.
@ref Rg 3 as amended by S 110/2008 (src:TA1999-RG3-S110-2008:16-21)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Third Schedule paragraphs 5 and 6 (deleted from 1 March 2008): the licensee is bound by the rate cap and the set-up charge allowance` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 3 2008) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `S 685/2011 (in operation 28 December 2011)`

-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:16 | In exercise of the powers conferred by section 74 of the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:17 | Telecommunications Act, the Info-communications Development
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:18 | Authority of Singapore, with the approval of the Minister for
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:19 | Information, Communications and the Arts, hereby makes the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:20 | following Regulations:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:22 | Citation and commencement
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:23 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:24 | (Class Licences) (Amendment) Regulations 2011 and shall come into
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:25 | operation on 28th December 2011.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:27 | Amendment of regulation 2
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:28 | 2. Regulation 2 of the Telecommunications (Class Licences)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:29 | Regulations (Rg 3) (referred to in these Regulations as the principal
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:30 | Regulations) is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:31 | (a) by deleting the definition of ‘‘class licence’’ and substituting
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:32 | the following definitions:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:33 | ‘‘ ‘‘Authority’’ means the Info-communications
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:34 | Development Authority of Singapore established
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:35 | under the Info-communications Development
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:36 | Authority of Singapore Act (Cap. 137A);
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:37 | ‘‘class licence’’ means a licence deemed to be granted
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:38 | under regulation 3;’’;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:41 | (b) by inserting, immediately after the definition of ‘‘Facilities-
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:42 | Based Operator’’, the following definition:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:43 | ‘‘ ‘‘Facilities-Based Operator licence’’ or ‘‘FBO licence’’
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:44 | means a licence specifically granted by the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:45 | to a Facilities-Based Operator under section 5 of
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:46 | the Act;’’; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:47 | (c) by deleting the definition of ‘‘specified telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:48 | systems and services’’ and substituting the following
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:49 | definitions:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:50 | ‘‘ ‘‘Services-Based Operator (Individual) licence’’ or ‘‘SBO
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:51 | (Individual) licence’’ means a licence specifically
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:52 | granted by the Authority to a Services-Based
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:53 | Operator under section 5 of the Act;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:54 | ‘‘specified telecommunication systems and services’’
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:55 | means the telecommunication systems and services
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:56 | described in the First, Second, Third, Fourth, Fifth,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:57 | Sixth, Seventh and Eighth Schedules.’’.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:59 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 3
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:60 | 3. Regulation 3 of the principal Regulations is deleted and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:61 | the following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:62 | ‘‘Class licence
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:63 | 3.—(1) An operator shall, upon compliance with regulations 4
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:64 | and 5, be deemed to have been granted a class licence under
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:65 | section 5 of the Act for the running of the types of specified
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:66 | telecommunication systems and services appropriate to the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:67 | telecommunication systems and services run by him.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:68 | (2) The class licence is granted subject to the conditions set
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:69 | out in the First, Second, Third, Fourth, Fifth, Sixth, Seventh or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:70 | Eighth Schedule, as the case may be.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:71 | (3) The holder of a FBO licence or SBO (Individual) licence
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:72 | shall not need a class licence for the running of any specified
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:73 | telecommunication systems or services which are specified in his
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:74 | FBO or SBO (Individual) licence.’’.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:76 | Amendment of regulation 5
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:77 | 4. Regulation 5 of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:78 | the word ‘‘Eighth’’ and substituting the word ‘‘Ninth’’.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:81 | New regulation 7A
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:82 | 5. The principal Regulations are amended by inserting, immediately
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:83 | after regulation 7, the following regulation:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:84 | ‘‘False or misleading information
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:85 | 7A.—(1) No person shall furnish any false, misleading or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:86 | inaccurate information to the Authority in relation to his
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:87 | registration under regulation 4.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:88 | (2) Any person who contravenes paragraph (1) shall be guilty
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:89 | of an offence.’’.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:91 | Amendment of First, Second, Third, Fourth, Fifth, Sixth and Seventh
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:92 | Schedules
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:93 | 6. The First, Second, Third, Fourth, Fifth, Sixth and Seventh
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:94 | Schedules to the principal Regulations are amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:95 | (a) by deleting the Schedule references and substituting the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:96 | following Schedule reference:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:97 | ‘‘Regulations 2 and 3’’; and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:98 | (b) by inserting, immediately after the word ‘‘complied’’ in
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:99 | the heading of paragraph 2, the word ‘‘with’’.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:101 | Deletion and substitution of Eighth Schedule and new Ninth Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:102 | 7. The Eighth Schedule to the principal Regulations is deleted and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:103 | the following Schedules substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:104 | ‘‘EIGHTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:105 | Regulations 2 and 3
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:106 | CLASS LICENCE FOR STORE-AND-FORWARD
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:107 | VALUE-ADDED NETWORK SERVICES
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:109 | Definition
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:110 | 1. The store-and-forward value-added network services are the services
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:111 | specified in paragraph 2 which have a value-added function at one end (such
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:112 | as the originating end) and are provided only on a call-by-call basis.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:114 | 2. The store-and-forward value-added network services referred to in
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:115 | paragraph 1 are any or both of the following:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:116 | (a) value-added data services being packet switched data services which
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:117 | convey end-to-end non-voice traffic by providing the value-added
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:118 | function of code and protocol conversion;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:121 | EIGHTH SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:123 | (b) value-added messaging services being value-added store-and-forward
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:124 | electronic messaging service, value-added store-and-forward facsimile,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:125 | value-added store-and-forward telex (excluding telegram) services and
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:126 | value-added store-and-forward voice mail services, that provide one
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:127 | or more of the following value-added store-and-forward functions on
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:128 | a non real-time basis:
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:129 | (i) deferred delivery;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:130 | (ii) multi-addressing;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:131 | (iii) content conversion;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:132 | (iv) format conversion, such as conversion from text-to-fax, text-to-
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:133 | telex, text-to-voice, fax-to-telex, fax-to-voice, telex-to-voice or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:134 | vice versa;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:135 | (v) processing of control information (such as destination address)
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:136 | with or without modification to the content;
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:137 | (vi) any other conversion that provides the users with additional,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:138 | different or restructured information.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:140 | Conditions to be complied with by licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:141 | 3. A licensee shall ensure that the value-added function is to be provided
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:142 | on a call-by-call basis.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:144 | 4. In the event that a licensee decides to terminate its value-added network
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:145 | services, it must notify the Authority in writing of its intent.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:147 | 5. A licensee must provide the store-and-forward value-added network
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:148 | services through —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:149 | (a) a service node in Singapore and, whenever requested by the Authority,
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:150 | make available the information on the routing table, subscriber
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:151 | database, call traffic statistics and other records maintained by the
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:152 | service node for inspection by the Authority; or
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:153 | (b) a local access node which is connected to the public switched
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:154 | telecommunication network provided by a FBO.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:156 | NINTH SCHEDULE
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:157 | Regulation 5
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:158 | REGISTRATION FEES FOR CLASS LICENCE
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:159 | PART I — FEES FOR TYPES OF CLASS LICENCES
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:161 | Licences Registration fees
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:162 | 1. Store-and-retrieve value-added network services —
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:163 | (a) where no leased circuits are used No fee
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:164 | (b) where leased circuits are used $200
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:167 | NINTH SCHEDULE — continued
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:169 | Licences Registration fees
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:170 | 2. Audiotex services $200
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:171 | 3. Resale of public switched telecommunication No fee
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:172 | services
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:173 | 4. Public chain payphone services No fee
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:174 | 5. Call-back and call re-origination services $200
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:175 | 6. Internet based voice and data services $200
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:176 | 7. International calling card services $200
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:177 | 8. Store-and-forward value-added network services $200.
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:180 | PART II — FEES WHERE CLASS LICENCES OVERLAP
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:182 | The maximum fee payable by an operator who runs specified telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:183 | systems and services falling within more than one class licence is $200.’’.
@ref Rg 3 as amended by S 685/2011 (src:TA1999-RG3-S685-2011:16-183)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licence is a licence deemed to be granted under regulation 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 2 (from 28 December 2011): this is a "class licence"` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 12 2011) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the licence is a licence deemed to be granted under regulation 3`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person holds a FBO licence or SBO (Individual) licence specifying the systems or services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 3(3) (from 28 December 2011): the holder needs a class licence for the systems or services` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 12 2011) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (NOT `the person holds a FBO licence or SBO (Individual) licence specifying the systems or services`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the person furnishes false, misleading or inaccurate information to the Authority in relation to registration under regulation 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 reg 7A (from 28 December 2011): the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 12 2011) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the person furnishes false, misleading or inaccurate information to the Authority in relation to registration under regulation 4`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the services are value-added data services (packet switched data services conveying end-to-end non-voice traffic with code and protocol conversion) or value-added messaging services with a store-and-forward function` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value-added function is provided on a call-by-call basis` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Eighth Schedule as substituted (from 28 December 2011): these are store-and-forward value-added network services provided under the class licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 12 2011) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the services are value-added data services (packet switched data services conveying end-to-end non-voice traffic with code and protocol conversion) or value-added messaging services with a store-and-forward function` AND `the value-added function is provided on a call-by-call basis`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee provides the services through a service node in Singapore (with the routing table, subscriber database, call traffic statistics and other records available to the Authority on request)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee provides the services through a local access node connected to the public switched telecommunication networks provided by a FBO` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee notified the Authority in writing of its intent to terminate the services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 3 Eighth Schedule items 4 and 5 (from 28 December 2011): the licensee is meeting the conditions` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 12 2011) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the licensee notified the Authority in writing of its intent to terminate the services` AND (`the licensee provides the services through a service node in Singapore (with the routing table, subscriber database, call traffic statistics and other records available to the Authority on request)` OR `the licensee provides the services through a local access node connected to the public switched telecommunication networks provided by a FBO`))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `type of class licence` IS A STRING
      `leased circuits are used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`Rg 3 Ninth Schedule Part I (from 28 December 2011): the registration fee` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 12 2011) THEN NOTHING
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Store-and-retrieve value-added network services" THEN (IF `leased circuits are used` THEN JUST "$200" ELSE JUST "No fee")
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Audiotex services" THEN JUST "$200"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Resale of public switched telecommunication services" THEN JUST "No fee"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Public chain payphone services" THEN JUST "No fee"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Call-back and call re-origination services" THEN JUST "$200"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Internet based voice and data services" THEN JUST "$200"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "International calling card service" THEN JUST "$200"
           IF `type of class licence` EQUALS "Store-and-forward value-added network services" THEN JUST "$200"
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 3 Ninth Schedule Part II (from 28 December 2011): the most an operator pays where its services fall within more than one class licence, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 28 12 2011) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST 200
